In article <10296@bloom-beacon.MIT.EDU> zam@athena.mit.edu (NorAazizam Bin MohdAasif) writes:
>	I am now on the 34th level and I had found the Amulet of
>Yendor on the 33th Level. (My version is 2.2) I am doubtful whether I
>have the original amulet since I didn't go into a lot of troubles
>trying to defeat the Wizard(1).  I had read the "Scrolls of Identify"
>to make sure that the amulet is not a fake one because I have come
>across some postings in this newsgroup regarding fake amulet.

If you saw the wizard, or if the scroll allowed you to identify it as the
"Amulet of Yendor" (and not "a cheap plastic imitation of the Amulet of
Yendor") then you have the real amulet.

>	I was told that one would find the amulet at least on the 40th
>level and my finding one on the 33th compounded my beliefs that it is
>not a genuine one.

Obviously, it is not always the case that the amulet will be below level 39.

> I am trying to go down to the deeper levels and I
>have been having some problems eversince.

Don't bother. Get out of the dungeon.

> After I had drunk the
>potion of confusion and had read the scroll of teleportation and have
>the ring of teleport control on, I couldn't go to the deeper levels
>and the message that I received was "You feel a bit disoriented".  I
>also received a lot of messages like "You yearn for your distance
>homeland" and "You feel worried about your your pets".  Does my pets
>have anything to do with it since I have four demons and one Demon
>Lord as my pets.  (I polymorphed myself into a demon and got some help
>when I was in trouble).

After you get the amulet, the wizard causes all sorts of strange things to
happen to you. One of these is that you are always feeling worried about
something or other. Another is that most of the time, your teleports don't
work but instead you "feel disoriented." Keep trying and the teleport will
eventually work (i'm not *certain* that this is so for level teleports, but
it is for normal ^T teleports).

